.TH SOCKRATES 1 "August 2026" "sockrates 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sockrates \- find open SOCKS5 proxies and make each one prove it works
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sockrates
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sockrates
collects SOCKS5 proxies from public lists and cross-examines every candidate until it
demonstrates that it reaches the target you care about. Finding proxies is trivial;
discarding the ones that do not work is the entire problem, so nothing is taken on the
proxy's word.
.PP
For TLS targets the handshake is completed
.I through
the proxy and the certificate is verified. For Telegram datacenters a real MTProto
handshake is performed and a valid
.B resPQ
carrying our own nonce is required. Every candidate is additionally asked to connect to an
unroutable address; anything reporting success there is discarded as a liar.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-target " NAME|HOST:PORT"
What the proxy must reach:
.BR telegram\-bot ", " telegram\-mtproto ", " https ,
or any
.IR host:port .
Default:
.BR telegram\-bot .
.TP
.BI \-\-cert\-contains " TEXT"
Require the TLS certificate to mention TEXT.
.TP
.BI \-\-in " FILE"
Re-test an existing list instead of downloading.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
Where to write. Default is standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " NAME"
One of
.BR plain ", " uri ", " csv ", " json ", " proxychains ", " python ", " curl .
.TP
.BI \-\-watch " MIN"
Never stop: re-hunt every MIN minutes and keep the output file true.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-latency " S"
Drop anything slower than S seconds.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-age " HOURS"
Only proxies known to have worked for at least this long.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-reliability " PCT"
Only proxies that passed at least PCT percent of past checks.
.TP
.B \-\-country ", " \-\-only\-country " CC"
Look up, and optionally filter by, country.
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " N" ", " \-\-timeout " S"
Concurrency (default 600) and per-proxy timeout (default 8).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-strict
Skip the liar control. Faster, worse results.
.TP
.B \-\-gui
Open the desktop application instead of running in the terminal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.sockrates/history.json
What has been observed about each proxy: when it was first seen working, how many checks it
has been through, and how many it passed.
.TP
.I ~/.sockrates.json
Last settings used by the desktop application.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Working proxies were found.
.TP
.B 1
Nothing to test.
.TP
.B 2
Tested, but nothing survived.
.TP
.B 3
The desktop app was requested but Tkinter is missing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Keep a file permanently true, refreshed every ten minutes:
.PP
.RS
.B sockrates \-\-target telegram\-mtproto \-\-watch 10 \-\-out live.txt
.RE
.PP
Only proxies with a day of history behind them, as a spreadsheet:
.PP
.RS
.B sockrates \-\-min\-age 24 \-\-min\-reliability 80 \-\-format csv \-\-out proven.csv
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation at
.UR https://github.com/SimuZSkyNeT/sockrates
.UE
